.description = "built-in widgets and how to write your own",
---

modules are the blocks you place into `slots`. each one is a directory
under `modules/` with an optional `generator.mjs` (runs at build time,
returns html), `client.js` (bundled into the site js) and `style.css`
(merged and purged).

# built-in

- `_header` - site title linking home
- `_theme_toggle` - light/dark switch
- `_lang_nav` - locale switcher, shows only other locales
- `_breadcrumbs` - home / section / page chain
- `_content` - the page body itself, required in `center`
- `_recents` - latest pages of a section + prev/next + random link;
  params: `section`, `count`, `title`, `show`, `id`
- `_explorer` - collapsible tree of every page
- `_footer_text` - copyright line from config
- `_rss_link` - rss badge when `features.rss` is on
- `_back_to_top` - scroll-to-top button

community modules without underscore: `badges` (88x31 buttons via
`items`), `divider`, `prev_next`, `search`, `social`, `spacer`.

# writing your own

```
modules/my-widget/
  generator.mjs   export default async ({ page, site, params, i18n }) => html
  client.js       plain script, bundled once per site
  style.css       merged with site css, unused rules purged
```

`params` are whatever you wrote next to `"module"` in the slot entry, so
one widget can be reused with different settings. need a module to act
differently on specific pages? copy it to `modules/search@/ru/` - the
suffix is a url-prefix override applied on top of base config.
